Q: How to show and update selected/unselected category for a product update page in CodeIgniter A: <p>Thanks for your support, and thanks who voted down my question. Here is my answer-</p>

<p>On controller :</p>

<pre><code>&lt;select class="form-control" name="categories[]" multiple&gt;
&lt;?php
    $product_id = "your product id";
    $category = $this-&gt;admin_product_model-&gt;getAllCat();
    foreach ($category as $row)
    {
        if( $this-&gt;admin_product_model-&gt;getCatByProductId($product_id,$row-&gt;cat_id) ){
            echo '&lt;option value="'.$row-&gt;cat_id.'" selected&gt;'.$row-&gt;cat_name.'&lt;/option&gt;';
        }else{
            echo '&lt;option value="'.$row-&gt;cat_id.'"&gt;'.$row-&gt;cat_name.'&lt;/option&gt;';
        }
    }
?&gt;
&lt;/select&gt;
</code></pre>

<p>This is only category select box section where $product_id = "your product id". I just call getAllCat() method from admin_product_model and when display it just check if the category already present on product_category table. If yes then add an attribute selected else show it as it is.</p>

<p>On admin_product_model model:</p>

<pre><code>//Get all category
function getAllCat(){
    $query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get('category')-&gt;result();
    return $query;
}
</code></pre>

<p>//This method check if product has this category</p>

<pre><code>function getCatByProductId($product_id,$cat_id){

    $this-&gt;db-&gt;from("product_cat");
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;where('product_id',$product_id);
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;where('cat_id',$cat_id);
    $query = $this-&gt;db-&gt;get();

    if($query-&gt;num_rows()&gt;=1){
        return TRUE;
    }
    else
    {
        return FALSE;
    }   
}
</code></pre>

<p>When user select or unselect category and other fields on product update page, the updateProduct method updated the all product related field to product table and check if update successful. If yes then delete all data of product_id from product_cat table and then loop through the $product_categories and insert the new value to product_cat table.</p>

<p>// update product</p>

<pre><code>function updateProduct($id,$product_categories)
{

// if all done just update new data to product
$data = array(
    ----your data to update product table----
);

$this-&gt;db-&gt;where('product_id',$id);
if($this-&gt;db-&gt;update('product',$data)){

    //Delete existing category
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;where('product_id', $id);
    $this-&gt;db-&gt;delete('product_cat');

    //store categories like this when user post data "$product_categories = $this-&gt;input-&gt;post('categories')"
    foreach ((array)$product_categories as $category)
    {
        $pc_data = array(
            'product_id' =&gt; $id,
